{
 "_": "How each weapon is held in first person, by your avatar's own hands (AvatarArms.luau). Each weapon has three looks (16 Nov 2026), and \"use\" picks one: before (place version 340: the guns near and big), after (place version 347: the Rivals layout, further off), combined (the owner: \"combine the new angles with the closer look\": before's size and nearness, the muzzle moved onto after's spot by the crosshair, Plan B and the Revolver turned to show their side). Flip one gun by changing its use; a Play test shows one look on every gun through the player's HoldLook attribute. looks.<name> = shift / scale / tilt / aimZ (below). katana.looks.<name>.rest = its rest pose; shredder.vm_looks.<name> = where the Shredder's first-person copy holds its grip and aims (camera space, studs). Per hand: pose = the kind of hold (grip / fist / cradle / wrap: the thing runs through the fist, at the hand's own grip attachment; palm: held from under; hand: the hand itself is the weapon, the Zombie Claw: placed whole at at (its middle), rot turning its own axes (x the back of the hand, y toward the wrist, z across), with tint = its colour (RGB) and the weapon's nail_ / cuff_ pieces refitted onto it, AvatarArms.fitOver), at = where the fist is on the weapon in the file's frame (metres, x right, y up, z back), rot = degrees about x, y, z (applied z first, like CFrame.Angles): +Y runs along the thing held, toward the thumb (a pistol grip: up it; a handguard: toward the muzzle, so -90 about x; palm: up into the thing); size = the hand against AvatarArms.HAND; elbow = this arm's own elbow spot; skins.<id>.R / L = a skin's (or a mode look's, the knife's spoon) own changes to that hand (its fields over the weapon's); turn = an extra turn about the handle, degrees. Each forearm runs from its wrist toward _elbow (camera space, metres). _size = how much larger than the web game's first-person scale every weapon (and the hands with it) is drawn: the owner, 16 Nov 2026, wanted bigger guns so the arms do not look long and lanky. scale = this weapon's size against _size; away = true: this hand waits off screen (hidden) and only comes in when a reload's off-hand track (Reloads lh) or a utility item calls it, the one-handed guns' left hand; shift = a move of the weapon's rest pose in camera space (metres, x right, y up, z back). Since 16 Nov 2026 (owner: look at how Rivals holds everything and match the look and sizes) both come from the Rivals-class measurements in the vault note 'Rivals first-person holds': every gun's muzzle sits just below and right of the crosshair (two-handed 55.5 / 58 % of the screen, one-handed 54.5 / 59), a two-handed gun covers about a quarter of the screen's width and leaves the bottom edge at about 80 % across, the Half a Shotgun reaches 67 %, a pistol 62 %; every gun is drawn at scale 1 (about the size it was; the hands with it, the same from gun to gun) and only the shift differs (the one-handed guns also have tilt, degrees about x, y, z added to their rest turn: 18 about y for Plan B, 24 for the Revolver; Half a Shotgun points straight ahead, so you see their side, not their back end): most guns sit about 0.35 m further from the camera than before, which is what makes them a quarter of the screen. The game's default FOV is 80. tools/roblox/hold_screen.py prints where each gun lands on a 16:9 screen. katana.vm = its rest and parry poses: where the guard is (camera space, metres), the way the blade points, and its roll (0 = edge down). ads = the aimed view (Viewmodel.adsPos, since 16 Nov 2026 place version 474): aimZ = the sight this much further from the eye (metres, on top of 0.17; the aim zoom's own push comes on top), sight = the aim line on the gun where its own Sight spot is blocked, kind = iron / dot / none / scope for the HUD, skins.<id> = a skin's own aimZ / sight, hide = its pieces (name prefixes) faded out while aiming, near = its big pieces by the stock drawn smaller in your own first-person view only (pieces, scale, pivot in file metres: the Seraph rifle's wings). Fitted with tools/roblox/hold_screen.py --ads / --hip. tools/roblox/holds.py writes roblox/src/shared/Holds.luau from this.",
